course: dictionary
lesson: 13223
title: One word, four meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word gallus is one of them. You will not know which meaning is right until you read the words around it. Those words are the context, and they leave clues.
explain: «Wee Rab was gallus, and he climbed the tallest tree in the park.» Climbing the tallest tree shows that Rab is daring and full of confidence. So in Scotland, gallus means bold and cheeky, often in a fun way.
explain: «The science book said the chicken is Gallus gallus domesticus.» Here gallus is not slang at all. It is a Latin scientific name, and the chicken belongs to the same group. «Grandad's galluses held up his old brown trousers» is a third meaning: galluses are braces, the straps that hold trousers up. Always check which meaning fits the sentence.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Gallus» in Scotland, especially Glasgow, means bold, cheeky and full of confidence, often in a fun, likeable way.
fact: «Gallus» in science is the Latin name for the group of jungle fowl that includes the chicken.
fact: «Galluses» is an old dialect word for braces, the straps that hold up trousers.
fact: Gallus is also a name: some Romans had it, and so did an early saint, Saint Gall.
exercise: «Wee Rab was gallus, and he climbed the tallest tree in the park.» What does gallus mean here? | Frightened of heights | Very tired after a long walk | *Bold and cheeky, full of confidence | A kind of bird, the chicken
exercise: In a science lesson, which name is the scientific name of the chicken? | *Gallus gallus domesticus | Gallus the bold | Galluses | Saint Gall
exercise: «Grandad's galluses held up his old brown trousers.» What are galluses? | Socks | *Braces, the straps that hold trousers up | Hats | Little dogs
test: Dad laughs and says, «Don't be so gallus, Ella, you'll fall off the wall!» What does gallus mean here? | A scientific name for a bird | Very hungry | Sleepy and calm | *Bold and cheeky
test: The teacher says, «Gallus is the name of a group of jungle fowl.» In which subject is gallus used? | Music | *Science | Football | Cooking
exam: Which sentence uses gallus to mean braces? | «The gallus was loud and cheeky in the playground.» | *«He wore galluses to keep his trousers up.» | «The gallus was a bright red bird in the jungle.» | «Gallus is a fun word to say.»
